course: dictionary
lesson: 8816
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many everyday words have more than one meaning, and sheet is one of them. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «Mum changed the bed sheets on Sunday.» Bed and changed tell you a sheet is a large cloth for a bed.
explain: «She wrote her answers on a sheet of paper.» Here a sheet is a thin flat piece of paper. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets, huge sheets of ice covering land.» The words huge and covering tell you a sheet can be a wide, flat layer of ice. The same word, three different meanings: the clues in each sentence show you which one to use.
fact: A sheet is a thin, flat piece of something.
fact: A sheet can be a piece of paper, a large cloth for a bed, or a flat piece of metal, glass or ice.
fact: A sheet of stamps or stickers is a set printed on one piece of paper.
fact: A worksheet is a page of school exercises.
fact: Without air in the way, heavy and light things fall at the same speed.
exercise: «She wrote her answers on a sheet of paper.» What is a sheet here? | A block of ice | *A thin flat piece of paper | A bed cover | A sticker
exercise: «Mum changed the bed sheets on Sunday.» What does sheets mean? | Layers of ice | Pages of school work | *Large cloths that cover a bed | Sets of stamps
exercise: Ben's worksheet has ten maths questions. What is a worksheet? | A sticker set | *A page of school exercises | A flat piece of ice | A large cloth for a bed
test: «A sheet of stamps is a set printed on one paper.» What does sheet mean in this sentence? | A thin cloth for a bed | *A set printed on one piece of paper | A layer of glass | A pile of books
test: «A sheet of paper laid flat on top of a book falls with it, because the book keeps the air off it.» Why does the paper fall with the book? | Because the paper is made of ice | *Because the book keeps the air off the paper | Because the book is wet | Because paper is heavier than books
exam: Which sentence uses sheet to mean a thin flat piece of metal? | The class finished their worksheet | Mum bought new cotton sheets for the bed | *The roof was covered with steel sheets | Sam printed a sheet of stickers for his book
